{"name":"Press Agent","hex":"#606b77","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"press agent","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who organizes the publicity for a firm or organization, and acts as an intermediary with the press and other media"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/press_agent"}],"entries":[{"title":"Publicity","blocks":[{"text":"In marketing, publicity is the public visibility or awareness for any product, service, person or organization. It may also refer to the movement of information from its source to the general public, often via the media. The subjects of publicity include people of public recognition, goods and services, organizations, and works of art or entertainment."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Publicity"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b9/Maggi_Arome_Pour_Corser_1895.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b9/Maggi_Arome_Pour_Corser_1895.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"French advertising poster \"Maggi arôme pour corser\" by Firmin Bouisset, circa 1895.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaggi_Arome_Pour_Corser_1895.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/17th_century_coffeehouse_england_1-580x400.jpg/500px-17th_century_coffeehouse_england_1-580x400.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/17th_century_coffeehouse_england_1-580x400.jpg/500px-17th_century_coffeehouse_england_1-580x400.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A coffeehouse in 17th century London.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A17th_century_coffeehouse_england_1-580x400.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/common